  "prompt": "/deep-research Which of the UK-born individuals who won The Nobel Prize in Economic Sciences while being affiliated with a UK based institution, between the inception of the award and the year that the first woman won The Nobel Prize in Economic Sciences, has fewer than 20 \"Articles\" listed on ideas.repec.org that have a publication year prior to the year that they won the award?",
  "prompt_prefix": "/deep-research ",
  "instruction": "Which of the UK-born individuals who won The Nobel Prize in Economic Sciences while being affiliated with a UK based institution, between the inception of the award and the year that the first woman won The Nobel Prize in Economic Sciences, has fewer than 20 \"Articles\" listed on ideas.repec.org that have a publication year prior to the year that they won the award?",
  "answer": "Based on my research, the answer is **Richard Stone (Nobel 1984)**.\n\n## Summary\n\n**UK-born, UK-affiliated Nobel Economics laureates (1969–2009):**\n| Laureate | Award Year | Birth Country | Affiliation at Award | Pre-award RePEc Articles |\n|----------|------------|---------------|---------------------|--------------------------|\n| John Hicks | 1972 | England | University of Oxford | ~30 |\n| James Meade | 1977 | England | University of Cambridge | 20 |\n| **Richard Stone** | **1984** | **England** | **University of Cambridge** | **18** |\n| Ronald Coase | 1991 | England | LSE / U. Chicago | 26 |\n| James Mirrlees | 1996 | Scotland | University of Cambridge | 25 |\n| Clive Granger | 2003 | Wales | UC San Diego (US) | — (not UK-affiliated) |\n\n**Richard Stone** is the only one with **fewer than 20 \"Articles\" on IDEAS/RePEc published strictly before his award year (1984)**. His profile shows 18 journal articles with publication years 1938–1982 (items 11–28 in the Articles list). The 1984 publications (items 8–10) are not counted since the criterion is \"publication year prior to the year that they won the award.\"\n\n## Sources\n- Nobel laureates list & affiliations: [Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Nobel_Memorial_Prize_laureates_in_Economic_Sciences) (verified against NobelPrize.org facts pages)\n- John Hicks RePEc: [ideas.repec.org/e/phi7.html](https://ideas.repec.org/e/phi7.html)\n- James Meade RePEc: [ideas.repec.org/e/pme25.html](https://ideas.repec.org/e/pme25.html)\n- Richard Stone RePEc: [ideas.repec.org/e/pst23.html](https://ideas.repec.org/e/pst23.html)\n- Ronald Coase RePEc: [ideas.repec.org/e/pco40.html](https://ideas.repec.org/e/pco40.html)\n- James Mirrlees RePEc: [ideas.repec.org/e/pmi20.html](https://ideas.repec.org/e/pmi20.html)\n- Clive Granger RePEc: [ideas.repec.org/e/pgr55.html](https://ideas.repec.org/e/pgr55.html)",
